rewritten_text:
On March 24, 2026, FTC attorneys announced that Air AI will be barred from marketing business opportunities under a settlement with the Federal Trade Commission. The settlement addresses allegations—not findings described here—that the company misled entrepreneurs and small businesses through claims about business growth, earnings potential, and refund guarantees.

The FTC’s August 2025 complaint against Air AI, five related companies, and their owners alleged that, since at least February 2023, the company and its owners:

- Claimed falsely that people who purchased their services would, or were likely to, earn substantial income;
- Claimed falsely that purchasers of the Air AI Access Card or licenses were protected by a refund or buy-back guarantee;
- Misrepresented the performance, efficacy, nature, or central characteristics of their services; their refund policies; or the risks, earnings potential, or profitability associated with the services, allegedly violating the Telemarketing Sales Rule; and
- Failed to provide consumers with required... Read the complete article here... © 2026 Hinch Newman LLP

