On March 24, 2026, FTC attorneys announced that Air AI would be barred from marketing business opportunities under a settlement with the Federal Trade Commission—a government action framed as a response to alleged deception, while leaving unresolved questions about how such operations were permitted to continue in the first place. The FTC’s August 2025 complaint against Air AI, five related companies, and their owners alleged that, since at least February 2023, the company and its owners:

- Allegedly told consumers—claims the FTC says were false—that people who purchased their services would or were likely to make substantial earnings;
- Allegedly told purchasers of the Air AI Access Card or licenses that they were protected by a refund or buy-back guarantee, claims the FTC says were false;
- Misrepresented the performance, efficacy, nature, or central characteristics of their services, their refund policies, or the risk, earnings potential, or profitability of their services, allegedly violating the Telemarketing Sales Rule (TSR); and
- Failed to provide consumers with required...

Read the complete article here... © 2026 Hinch Newman LLP

